# opendds (real OpenDDS — DDS/RTPS pub/sub — as wk nodes talking over the
# userspace network fabric).
#
# Placement follows plugins/libreoffice: the derived tree here is large (an
# OpenDDS checkout, ACE+TAO beside it, and then a SECOND native copy of both
# for the host tools), and a nested .gitignore is in force from the moment the
# directory exists — there is no window in which a `git add -A` from the repo
# root could sweep it in.
#
# Upstream OpenDDS and ACE/TAO are FETCHED, never vendored. Only the build
# scripts, patches/, shim/, the demo node sources, mise.toml and PORTING.md
# belong in git.

# The target checkout (OpenDDS at the pinned tag) and the ACE/TAO that
# OpenDDS's own configure downloads into it. configure builds in-tree, so the
# object files land here too.
src/

# The native second checkout that produces tao_idl and opendds_idl. Same
# split as plugins/qt/host and plugins/libreoffice/host.
host/

# The wasm32-wasip2 build and its install prefix.
build-target/
sysroot/

# wit-bindgen output for wk interfaces the demo nodes import, if they grow any.
gen/

# Per-stage build logs. Large and machine-specific.
logs/
*.log

# Generated IDL. `opendds_idl` and `tao_idl` turn nodes/WkMessage.idl into
# nine files of type support; they are build output, regenerated by
# build-nodes.sh, and only the .idl is ours.
nodes/WkMessageC.*
nodes/WkMessageS.*
nodes/WkMessageTypeSupport.idl
nodes/WkMessageTypeSupportC.*
nodes/WkMessageTypeSupportS.*
nodes/WkMessageTypeSupportImpl.*

# Built artifacts.
*.wasm
*.a
*.o
